# SYNTHETIC — hand-written from RFC 1939 §3, not a recording.
# The phase-0 capture against a real server has not happened yet.
# "..a line that starts with a dot" must be delivered with one leading dot,
# and ".." as a line containing only a dot. The bare "." line is the
# terminator and is not part of the message.

S: +OK POP3 server ready
C: RETR 1
S: +OK 80 octets
S: From: ada@example.test
S: Subject: dots
S:
S: Hello
S: ..a line that starts with a dot
S: ..
S: Bye
S: .
C: QUIT
S: +OK bye
DONE
